  "plot_summary": "[HANG0] * Paul Gambaccini's letter printed in [LINK:1963:ASM_7|ASM #7] was perhaps the first case of calling the competition \"echh\" - that's a phrase we'll be hearing more of!\n\n[HANG0] * The Announcements at the end of [LINK:1963:ASM_7|ASM #7] actually asks permission to <i>discontinue the letters page</i> in ASM, indicating that it takes a good while to put together and suggests that comments about <i>all</i> magazines be instead directed to the FF mag, indicating:&nbsp; <i>We'll do nothing till we hear from you, so let us know.&nbsp; But, as a special favor, we hope you'll tell us you don't mind.</i>  (Boy, I'll get <i>that</i> went over like a lead balloon - <i>wow</i>!)\n\n[ASSET: right | AvengersNextIssue | width=21%] [HANG0] * In light of Iron Man's new armor introduced in this month's [LINK:1963:TOS_48_iron0|TOS #48], the full-page ad in this month's [LINK:1963:AVEN_2|AVEN #2] already looks stale.\n[BR]\n[BR] It correctly indicates that the Sub-Mariner will feature in the next issue, but still shows Iron Man wearing his older armor.&nbsp; You can clearly see which issue was published first, the ad presumably drawn before it was known that Iron Man would redesign his suit.&nbsp; (For the record, AVEN #3 does not get published until November, a full two months after this month's issue 2.)\n[BR]\n[BR] [SPAN: fontsize=small; text=(And since <i>Avengers</i> is a title, the word should be the singular \"<b>features</b>\" rather than \"feature,\" but let's not get nit-picky, because then I'd have to point out that the Hulk's head shouldn't be there... because he just <i>quit</i>!&nbsp; And I <i>really</i> don't want to have to do that, <i>wink...</i>)]",
