  "review_text": "Nine graded stories spread over eight issues this month, with a weighted average of [SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx]\n\n<b>FIXME</b>\n\n, which was just over half a point better than last month's <b>4.79</b>.&nbsp; This was particularly surprising due to the <i>dreadful</i> abomination of the <i>Avengers</i> this month, complete with unimpressive outings by the <i>X-Men</i> and <i>Fantastic Four</i> as well. Thankfully they were offset in large measure by a solid Spider-Man entry and even stronger-than-normal outings by the Human Torch and Iron Man.&nbsp; Even the origin of Dr. Strange played its part in keeping this month's issues above reader-level as a whole.&nbsp; It was a close call, however.\n\nI was also pleased by the TO BE CONTINUED ending in TTA.&nbsp; It wasn't the \"cliff-hanger\" where someone is falling to their doom or an explosion apparently kills our hero - the villain was actually far away from the heroes - but it was encouraging that the \"training wheels\" are coming off, and Lee and his collaborators are feeling confident enough now that the audience will be back next month to scoop up the next issue to see what happens.&nbsp; Very encouraging sign!&nbsp; And note that the letters page of [LINK:1963:FF_21|FF #21] even asks readers if they'd like to \"see more two-part tales like this one!\" (referring to [LINK:1963:TTA_50_giant0|TTA #50])\n\nHighlights:\n[HANG0] * [LINK:1963:JIM_98_thor0|JIM #98]'s last panel on page 9, complete with a battle cry on the part of Thor - <i>well done</i> - and absolutely the best panel of the month!\n[HANG0] * Introduction of the Space Phantom, Cobra, Human Top and Vanisher\n[HANG0] * Guest appearance by Nick Fury in the FF (in the present no less)\n[HANG0] * New Iron Man armor transitions him closer to his more familiar look\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.58 grade character issue   weight 6.0   thor      JIM #98 0.50 6.0   asm       ASM #7  1.00 5.5   strange   ST #115 0.33 5.0   giant     TTA #50 0.50 5.0   torch     ST #115 0.50 5.0   iron      TOS #48 0.75 4.0   ff        FF #21  1.00 3.0   xmen      XMEN #2 1.00 1.8   aven      AVEN #2 1.004.31*** LAST MONTH ***7 graded stories over 6 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 4.75 grade character issue   weight 6.0   asm       ASM #6  1.00 6.0   ff        FF #20  1.00 6.0   iron      TOS #47 0.75 5.0   torch     ST #114 0.75 2.5   giant     TTA #49 0.50 2.0   strange   ST #114 0.25 1.5   thor      JIM #97 0.504.79\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nSpace Phantom | villain | Milestone: (first)\nCobra | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nWhirlwind | villain | Milestone: (first: as Human Top)\nVanisher | villain | Milestone: (first)\nNotes | first | Fred Duncan\nHate-Monger | villain | Milestone: (first)\nNick Fury | Milestone: (identity: first time as \"Colonel Fury\")\nNotes | first | villain | Mr. Doll (Nathan Dolly)\nNotes | first | Mark II Armor (Red and Gold)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * The Avengers stumble through a Space Phantom fiasco so messy you can't help rubbernecking the wreck.\n[HANG0] * A slithering foe and a returning nurse can't distract Thor from rediscovering the joy of battle.\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * But <i>most importantly</i>, Jeff reviewed his <b>100<sup>th</sup></b> issue this month!\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "[HANG0] * Thor has yet <i>another</i> new menace to deal with\n[HANG0] * Hank and Jan take the next step toward trying to stop their whirling enemy\n[HANG0] * New powers for the Invisible Girl\n[HANG0] * Ben and Johnny battle each <i>other</i>\n[HANG0] * Iron Man meets X-Men's Angel\n[HANG0] * And what's <i>this</i>?&nbsp; Peter Parker boxing with Flash Thompson?&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=warning; fonttype=bold-italic; text=Whoa!]"
